---
description: Keep code comments and PR descriptions concise; don't over-explain
alwaysApply: true
---

# Concise comments and PR descriptions

Prefer self-explanatory code over commentary. Only comment non-obvious intent,
trade-offs, or constraints that the code itself can't convey.

- Don't add comments that restate what the code does.
- Don't narrate the change or the decisions that led to it in comments.
- If the code is self-explanatory, leave it uncommented.

PR descriptions are for human reviewers — a short, high-level sense of the change.

- Don't enumerate every code change or walk through the diff.
- A brief summary plus the "why" is enough.
